ord, but also in the sight of men.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªAnd we have sent with them our brother, whom we have oftentimes proved diligent in many things, but now much more diligent, upon the great confidence which I have in you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´Whether any do enquire of Titus, he is my partner and fellowhelper concerning you: or our brethren be enquired of, they are the messengers of the churches, and the glory of Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoWherefore shew ye to them, and before the churches, the proof of your love, and of our boasting on your behalf.¦layout ªlast_verse